        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0879" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg817"/>

                <head>No. 482.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mantilla to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain in Washington</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26, 1878</date>.
                        (Received June 27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of His Catholic
                    Majesty, affected by the most profound feelings, performs the sad duty of
                    communicating to the honorable Secretary of State of the United States, for the
                    information of the President of the Republic and of the government of which he
                    is the head, that he has just received a telegram from the minister of state of
                    His Majesty the <pb facs="0880" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/> King of Spain,
                    notifying him of the death, at a quarter past twelve o’clock to-day, of Her
                    Majesty the Queen, Doña Maria de las Mercedes de Orleans y Borbon, resulting
                    from a nervous gastric fever.</p>
                <p>Upon this sad occasion the undersigned has the honor of renewing, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ANTONIO MANTILLA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
